1
00:00:02,119 --> 00:00:07,319
today, no animal had killed another animal. Not even a rat had been killed.

2
00:00:07,319 --> 00:00:10,720
They had made the

3
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:16,119
They had made their way onto the little knoll where the half-finished windmill

4
00:00:16,119 --> 00:00:22,239
stood. And with one accord, they all lay down as though huddling together for warmth.

5
00:00:22,239 --> 00:00:29,720
Clover, Muriel, Benjamin, the cows, the sheep, and a whole flock of geese and hens.

6
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:34,439
Everyone, indeed, except the cat, who had suddenly disappeared just before

7
00:00:34,439 --> 00:00:37,760
Napoleon ordered the animals to assemble.

8
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:40,640
For some time, nobody spoke.

9
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:46,600
Only Boxer remained on his feet. He fidgeted to and fro, swishing his long

10
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:52,159
black tail against his sides, and occasionally uttering a little whinny of surprise.

11
00:00:52,159 --> 00:00:58,399
Finally, he said, >> "I do not understand it. I would not have believed that such things could

12
00:00:58,399 --> 00:01:00,319
happen on our farm.

13
00:01:00,319 --> 00:01:03,319
It must be due to some fault in ourselves.

14
00:01:03,319 --> 00:01:07,359
The solution, as I see it, is to work harder.

15
00:01:07,359 --> 00:01:12,600
From now onwards, I shall get up a full hour earlier in the mornings."

16
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:17,520
>> And he moved off at his lumbering trot and made for the quarry.

17
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:22,119
Having got there, he collected two successive loads of stone and dragged

18
00:01:22,119 --> 00:01:25,960
them down to the windmill before retiring for the night.

19
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:29,880
The animals huddled about Clover, not speaking.

20
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:35,039
The knoll where they were lying gave them a wide prospect across the countryside.

21
00:01:35,039 --> 00:01:38,239
Most of Animal Farm was within their view.

22
00:01:38,239 --> 00:01:43,680
The long pasture, stretching down to the main road, the hayfield, the spinney,

23
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:48,479
the drinking pool, the plowed fields where the young wheat was thick and

24
00:01:48,479 --> 00:01:55,600
green, and the red roofs of the farm buildings with the smoke curling from the chimneys.

25
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:58,279
It was a clear spring evening.

26
00:01:58,279 --> 00:02:03,920
The grass and the bursting hedges were gilded by the level rays of the sun.

27
00:02:03,920 --> 00:02:08,159
Never had the farm, and with a kind of surprise they remembered that it was

28
00:02:08,159 --> 00:02:15,079
their own farm, every inch of it their own property, appeared to the animals so desirable a

29
00:02:15,079 --> 00:02:16,680
place.

30
00:02:16,680 --> 00:02:21,720
As Clover looked down the hillside, her eyes filled with tears.

31
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:25,800
If she could have spoken her thoughts, it would have been to say that this was

32
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:31,000
not what they had aimed at when they had set themselves years ago to work for the

33
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,960
overthrow of the human race.

34
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:39,239
These scenes of terror and slaughter were not what they had looked forward to

35
00:02:39,239 --> 00:02:44,359
on that night when old Major first stirred them to rebellion.

36
00:02:44,359 --> 00:02:49,560
If she herself had had any picture of the future, it had been of a society of

37
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:53,600
animals set free from hunger and the whip.

38
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:59,079
All equal, each working according to his capacity, the strong protecting the

39
00:02:59,079 --> 00:03:04,560
weak, as she had protected the lost brood of ducklings with her foreleg on

40
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:07,520
the night of Major's speech.

41
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:13,359
Instead, she did not know why, they had come to a time when no one dared speak

42
00:03:13,359 --> 00:03:19,359
his mind, when fierce, growling dogs roamed everywhere, and when you had to

43
00:03:19,359 --> 00:03:25,640
watch your comrades torn to pieces after confessing to shocking crimes.

44
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:30,520
There was no thought of rebellion or disobedience in her mind.

45
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:35,039
She knew that even as things were, they were far better off than they had been

46
00:03:35,039 --> 00:03:40,199
in the days of Jones, and that before all else, it was needful to prevent the

47
00:03:40,199 --> 00:03:43,279
return of the human beings.

48
00:03:43,279 --> 00:03:48,199
Whatever happened, she would remain faithful, work hard, carry out the

49
00:03:48,199 --> 00:03:53,479
orders that were given to her, and accept the leadership of Napoleon.

50
00:03:53,479 --> 00:04:00,960
But still, it was not for this that she and all the other animals had hoped and toiled.

51
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:07,960
It was not for this that they had built the windmill and faced the bullets of Jones's gun.

52
00:04:07,960 --> 00:04:12,880
Such were her thoughts, though she lacked the words to express them.

53
00:04:12,880 --> 00:04:17,760
At last, feeling this to be in some way a substitute for the words she was

54
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:23,600
unable to find, she began to sing Beasts of England.

55
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:27,800
The other animals sitting round her took it up, and they sang it three times

56
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:35,560
over, very tunefully, but slowly and mournfully, in a way they had never sung it before.

57
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:39,359
They had just finished singing it for the third time when Squealer, attended

58
00:04:39,359 --> 00:04:44,000
by two dogs, approached them with the air [clears throat] of having something important to say.
